  "result": "Perfect! All 106 tests pass. I've successfully created a dates module for UTC-based date operations:\n\n**New `src/dates.js` with three functions:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates date strings:\n   - Must be in YYYY-MM-DD format\n   - Must represent a real date (handles leap years, non-existent dates like Feb 30)\n   - Rejects invalid formats and out-of-range values\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds days to a date:\n   - Takes a YYYY-MM-DD string\n   - Adds n days (can be negative for subtraction)\n   - Returns YYYY-MM-DD string\n   - Works across year and month boundaries\n   - All arithmetic in UTC\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Calculates whole days between dates:\n   - Returns b minus a in whole days\n   - Can be negative if a > b\n   - Works across boundaries\n   - All arithmetic in UTC\n\n**Updated `createInvoice()`:**\n- Now uses `isValidDate()` from dates.js (removed local duplicate)\n- Ensures date validation is consistent across the system\n\n**Key design decision:**\n- All dates work in UTC with 'YYYY-MM-DD' strings\n- No local timezone conversions\u2014dates are parsed with 'T00:00:00Z'\n- Date arithmetic uses UTC methods (getUTCDate, setUTCDate, etc.)\n\n**Tests added (14 new):**\n- Format validation (valid/invalid formats, non-existent dates)\n- Leap year handling (2000, 2024 leap years; 1900, 2025 non-leap)\n- addDays with positive, negative, and zero values\n- Boundary crossing (year/month changes)\n- daysBetween in both directions and across boundaries\n- Large date ranges (full year calculations)",
